<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afrikaners</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Afrikaner</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Afrikaners are a South African people descended mainly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settlers, together with German and French Huguenot immigrants, who arrived after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> founded the Cape settlement in 1652. They developed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> language from Dutch. They are one of the lasting legacies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
